<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#ndlovukati">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ndlovukati</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ndlovukati, meaning she-elephant, is the title of the queen mother of the Swazi Kingdom (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eswatini">Eswatini</a>). She rules jointly with the king, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngwenyama">Ngwenyama</a>, keeping her own royal village at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lobamba">Lobamba</a>, taking part in national rituals such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incwala">Incwala</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umhlanga">Umhlanga</a>, and acting as a check on royal power. When the king is a minor, the Ndlovukati or another senior queen may act as regent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ndlovukati.jpg" alt="Ndlovukati" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RoyFocker 12 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Eswatini.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
